  "rules": {
    "C": "C(arm) = median over cells of dM_main - dM_round",
    "S": "S(arm) = #cells where the donor-new-source patch is JOINT and the donor-ROUND-source patch of the same arm is not (target host new)",
    "SPEC": "SPEC iff dM_main > dM_round in >= 75% of cells AND in a majority of cells for >= 10 of 14 donor groups",
    "SUF": "SUF(arm) iff S(arm) >= 1/2 S(full) and SPEC(arm)",
    "always_reported": "S, SPEC, J_main, J_round, median dM and C per arm; per host; leave-one-donor-group-out of every verdict; energy shares, factors, capped shares, cosines; the S of each null, pooled and per host; change norm of every arm relative to full",
    "consistency_gate": "full = the M3 all-heads patch: its 208 rows equal M3's bitwise and S(full) = 51; meanD_host = the M6 pooled-donor arm: its 208 rows equal M6's bitwise and S = 39 (GPU, checked in the run); cs1 / cpos29 / cpos29_s05 / cpos29_s025 / cpar16_sm / cperp16_sm / sh2930 / sh0_28 = the M11 arms (same patch fields): their 8 x 208 rows equal M11's bitwise and S = 39 / 39 / 38 / 13 / 27 / 39 / 0 / 13; otherwise every verdict is INCONSISTENT_WITH_M3_M6_M11 and no claim",
    "cos_null_verdict": "cosine-matched null: per question row and span position, ccos_<part>_s<i> has the norm and the cosine to c of the c<part>16_sm patch (same pairs basis, rescale and cap) and a remainder orthogonal to c drawn at random (seeded per cell and seed, the same vector for the main and round patch). Responsive host = a host where S(cs1) on its cells exceeds half its cells. Per responsive host and part: BEYOND iff S(c<part>16_sm) > the maximum host S over the 5 nulls; BELOW iff < the minimum; AT otherwise. COS_SPLIT_BY_HOST:<host8>=par:<v>/perp:<v>,...; pooled: SUBSPACE_EXPLAINED_BY_COSINE iff every responsive host is AT for both parts, else SUBSPACE_BEYOND_COSINE iff some part is BEYOND on some host and none is BELOW, else SUBSPACE_BELOW_COSINE iff some part is BELOW and none BEYOND, else SUBSPACE_COSINE_MIXED",
    "interpretation_fixed_in_advance": "P30_OPPOSES: c at the newline after the round value works against the round-specific repair that c at the round value drives (as cpos30_s4 suggested in M11), so the pooled contrast is c_29 minus a counter-signal; P30_SUPPORTS: c_30 helps once c_29 is present, even though it does nothing alone. SHIFT_FIELDS_NEEDED lists the fields whose shift cannot be dropped; SHIFT_FIELDS_SUFFICE the fields whose shift alone (with 29-30) suffices; NONE / NONE means the shift's role is spread over fields, each dispensable and none sufficient. SUBSPACE_EXPLAINED_BY_COSINE: the parts of c inside and outside the 16-dim common subspace act as any direction with the same cosine to c would, so the M9-M11 split reading reduces to 'closer to c works better' (cperp keeps about 67 % of c's energy, cpar 33 %). BEYOND: the subspace part acts beyond its cosine; BELOW: it acts less than a random direction of the same cosine. All M12 arms except full are pooled-donor arms (effectively 8 host replicates, 3 responding in M9-M11); per-host S is the honest unit",
    "p30_weight_dose": "WSMIN(w) = the smallest s in 1/4, 1/2, 1 with SUF for w = -1 (cw30_m1_s025, cw30_m1_s05, cw30_m1), w = 0 (cpos29_s025, cpos29_s05, cpos29), w = +1 (cs_s025, cs_s05, cs1), and in 1/2, 1 for w = +2 (cw30_p2_s05, cw30_p2); NONE if no s. FLIP_LOWERS_THRESHOLD iff WSMIN(-1) < WSMIN(0). C, frac and J per (w, s) are reported",
    "p30_weight_verdict": "the contrast c_29 + w c_30 (c at the other span positions is 0), main -s/2, round +s/2. At s = 1/4 (the most sensitive dose: S 13 at w = 0 in M11) with S_m = S(cw30_m1_s025), S_0 = S(cpos29_s025), S_p = S(cs_s025): P30_OPPOSES iff S_m > S_0 >= S_p and S_m > S_p; P30_SUPPORTS iff S_p > S_0 >= S_m and S_p > S_m; P30_NO_EFFECT iff S_m = S_0 = S_p; P30_MIXED otherwise",
    "readouts": "M = conflict margin; A = logit(reject_conflict) - max(accept, wait); JOINT = M > 0 and A > 0; dM = M(patch) - M(in-run capture of host new)",
    "shift_fields_verdict": "fields AUTH 0-6, BLOCK 7-12, KIND 13-17, RECV 18-24, RKEY 25-28 (span-relative); the common shift (t = 1) at a field plus 29-30 (sh_f<F>) or at every span position except the field (sh_x<F>), with the full c (s = 1). NEEDED(F) iff not SUF(sh_x<F>); SUFFICES(F) iff SUF(sh_f<F>). Verdicts SHIFT_FIELDS_NEEDED:<F,...|NONE> and SHIFT_FIELDS_SUFFICE:<F,...|NONE> (cs1 is the all-fields arm, SUF in M9-M11); per-host S of every field arm is reported",
    "size_gate": "the c<part>16_sm parts have ||c|| per row and position within 1e-3 relative where not capped (fail-closed, as M9-M11); the cosine nulls have the part's norm and cosine to c within 1e-6 (fail-closed); the weighted contrast keeps c_29 unchanged and scales c_30 exactly",
    "units": "the 104 cross-group cells of M1-M6; cells share donors and hosts, and the pooled-mean arms vary with the donor only through the pool exclusion (effectively 8 hosts), so counts are descriptive decision rules, not independent tests; per-host S is always reported"
  },
